        "id": "p0",
        "title": "Guard Points",
        "text": "Some attacks briefly BLOCK an incoming strike and keep on going - that protected part is called a guard point, or autoguard. It's not armor: normals deal no damage through it, Specials still chip, and every move has its own guard-point timing."
      },
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "title": "Recognize Them",
        "text": "Ayu {input:6C} is your practice tool here. Misaki {input:5C}, {input:236B}, and {input:66C} are three more guard-point attacks worth learning to spot. They all guard as though STANDING - so a well-timed low slips right under the protection."
      }
    ],
    "tasks": [
      {
        "id": "use_gp",
        "kind": "combat",
        "label": "Use Ayu {input:6C} to block the cued strike and continue",
        "sequence": [
          {
